* Class A 30 W power amp ("AC30 Top Boost" reissue, Vox drawing AC30-60-02 issue 5, sheet 2): V6 12AX7 long-tailed
* phase inverter (1k2 + 47k tail, 1M grid returns), four EL84 as two parallel pairs on a shared cathode bias
* (two 100 ohm / 5 W in parallel, 220u), no negative feedback, the 4k output transformer, and the supply: GZ34
* rectifier, 47u reservoir (node a, integrated by the engine), choke, 22u (node b = HT).
*
* Assumptions where the drawing is silent or ambiguous (change them here, not in code):
*  - the drawing prints no voltages: the supply (mains transformer 789-102) is a Thevenin rectifier source chosen
*    for an HT of about 340 V at idle;
*  - output transformer 784-413: 4k plate-to-plate onto the 16 ohm tap with the two 8 ohm speakers in series,
*    6 H per primary half, 50 ohm per half, coupling like the other amps;
*  - the choke CH1 is 10 H with 100 ohm of winding resistance (the drawing prints only its part number, 292-767);
*  - the phase inverter's right grid goes to the Vib/Trem bus through C2 (4n7): taken as a ground return;
*  - Cut: 4n7 + 220k rheostat between the two grid lines; the knob turns the resistance down.

.nodes pin gl gr nt kv pa pb y ga gb g1 g2 cn a b x pt pbm npt npb s1 s2 kc t16

S VAUDIO pin 150k 0
S VHT a 15 345

* Phase inverter V6: signal on the left grid through C3 (47n), the right grid returned through C2 (4n7).
C C3 pin gl 47n
R R4 gl nt 1M
C C2 gr 0 4n7
R R2 gr nt 1M
R R3 kv nt 1k2
R R1 nt 0 47k
T V6A gl pa kv 12AX7
T V6B gr pb kv 12AX7
R R52 y pa 100k
R R51 y pb 100k
R R54 b y 22k
C C35 y 0 10u

* Coupling to the EL84 grids (100n, 220k leaks to ground, 1k5 stoppers, two tubes per side) and Cut.
C C25 pa ga 100n
C C24 pb gb 100n
R R50 ga 0 220k
R R53 gb 0 220k
R RS_A ga g1 1k5/2
R RS_B gb g2 1k5/2
C C1 ga cn 4n7
R VR_CUT cn gb 220k

* EL84: V3 + V2 on one half of the primary, V4 + V5 on the other; common cathode 50 ohm || 220u.
P V3 g1 pt s1 kc EL84 2
P V4 g2 pbm s2 kc EL84 2
R R70 kc 0 100/2
C C47 kc 0 220u
R R75 b s1 100/2
R R77 b s2 100/2

* Output transformer: primary halves around the HT centre tap, one 16 ohm secondary.
R DCR_PT pt npt 50
R DCR_PB pbm npb 50
.param n16 = 2*1/sqrt(4000/16)
* Core saturation: SAT is the flux (volt-seconds) where the extra magnetising current equals the linear one; ~full-power
* plate-to-plate swing / (2 pi f), with f about 28-30 Hz for the large Marshall / Soldano / Peavey / Fender cores, 50 to 65 Hz for the small AC30 / tweed cores.
.xfmr OT L=6 SAT=1.6
  W npt b 1 pri
  W b npb 1 pri
  W t16 0 n16 sec
  K pri pri 0.9998
  K pri sec 0.9993
.end
R RLOAD t16 0 16

* Supply: the choke CH1 (10 H, 100 ohm) and 22u after the reservoir; x is HT for the preamp, RPREAMP its draw.
R CH1 a ch 100
.xfmr CHOKE L=10
  W ch b 1 ch
.end
C C46 b 0 22u
R RX b x 1
R RPREAMP x 0 75k
